00:34:47.850 --> 00:34:50.670
you click on Run
Job, what's happening

00:34:50.670 --> 00:34:53.070
is that Dataprep is taking
that recipe, the steps that

00:34:53.070 --> 00:34:55.230
are defined inside that
recipe, translating that

00:34:55.230 --> 00:34:59.220
into a Dataflow job that
you saw on the screen that

00:34:59.220 --> 00:35:00.960
went through the execution.

00:35:00.960 --> 00:35:08.190
That Dataflow job reads source
data from your GCP project,

00:35:08.190 --> 00:35:11.580
transforms that data
within your GCP project

00:35:11.580 --> 00:35:13.545
and writes it back out
into the same project.

00:35:13.545 --> 00:35:14.170
CORI PEELE: OK.

00:35:14.170 --> 00:35:15.750
SEAN MA: So actually
the data always stays

00:35:15.750 --> 00:35:17.460
within that project
and doesn't leave it.

00:35:17.460 --> 00:35:20.070
And all the processing
is done there.

00:35:20.070 --> 00:35:22.292
In terms of storage
of data, Dataprep

00:35:22.292 --> 00:35:24.750
itself doesn't store any data,
because what you're actually

00:35:24.750 --> 00:35:26.130
seeing-- what we're
doing is we're actually

00:35:26.130 --> 00:35:28.065
asking Dataflow to
actually run the processing

00:35:28.065 --> 00:35:29.400
and generate the new dataset.

